{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1082", "sample_idx": 44, "model_name": "mistralai/ministral-14b-instruct-2512", "content": "Liam jolted awake to the hum of processors and the shimmer of neon reflections dancing on his eyelids. His hands hovered an inch above his bedsheets, fingers twitching against an invisible boundary. The room—once a cozy, cluttered apartment—now pulsed with digital energy, its walls flickering between concrete textures and pixelated glitches. A floating health bar materialized above his head, and when he reached for his nightstand, his fingers passed through a glowing orb that read *\"Objective: Survive.\"* A distant voice crackled like a corrupted radio signal: *\"Player detected. Welcome to the simulation.\"* Panic clawed at his throat as he remembered the last thing he’d done before bed—an online forum post about \"glitches in reality.\" The mirror across the room didn’t reflect him; instead, it displayed a loading screen with his name embossed at the top.\n\nOutside, the city stretched endlessly, buildings stacked like infinite Lego blocks, their edges jagged with unresolved polygons. Liam sprinted through the streets, dodging NPCs who ignored him or blinked in and out of existence. A clock tower chimed erratically, its hands spinning backward, and a street sign flickered between \"Main Street\" and \"??? Level.\" He stumbled into a café where patrons sipped from mugs labeled *\"Exp: +50.\"* A bartender slid a menu across the counter: *\"Choose your stat boost—Strength, Agility, or Sanity.\"* As Liam traced the options with a trembling finger, a notification flashed: *\"Warning: Reality drift detected. 10% chance of permanent desynchronization.\"* Behind the counter, a shadowy figure in a developer’s hoodie smirked. \"You’re doing great,\" it said. \"But the boss fight starts at dawn.\"", "logprobs": [{"token": "L", "logprob": -1.3595261573791504}, {"token": "iam", "logprob": -0.035708848387002945}, {"token": " j", "logprob": -0.60082948